  "captions": [
    {
      "name": "fig_reference_rd",
      "caption": "Left: means across all 100 crops at each of five native QPs, joined only as visual guides. Right: per-image log-rate linear interpolation and paired quality differences on the four-model common support at each rate; n is explicit and can change with rate. Whiskers are 95% image-bootstrap intervals conditional on the frozen checkpoints and included cohort. D2/D4/D6 are epoch20 of105; D12 is released and is not a matched-training causal depth control. Rates are actual rANS payload, excluding the custom research header. Figure notes: Actual coded rate \u00b7 frozen epoch-20 models 100 DIV2K centre crops \u00b7 CPU FP32 \u00b7 D12 has different training provenance \u00b7 paired-image 95% intervals"
    },
    {
      "name": "fig_reference_coverage",
      "caption": "At0.2 actual payload bpp, compare the original monitor images0801\u20130804 with the remaining validation images, restricting both groups to the four-model common support. The small monitor subset receives no confidence interval. The coverage panel reports pairwise and four-model shared support at each rate, preventing silent extrapolation or an implicit claim that every rate uses all100 images. Figure notes: Validation coverage Means use common supported images \u00b7 no interval estimated for the four-crop subset \u00b7 cohorts vary with bitrate"
    },
    {
      "name": "fig_reference_rate_accounting",
      "caption": "Left: mean actual rANS payload minus estimated entropy with pointwise95% image-bootstrap intervals. Right: average per-image BD-rate relative to releasedD12; PCHIP log-rate integration is restricted to each image\u2019s four-model common PSNR interval, and nonmonotone curves are rejected. n reports valid images. The custom88-byte header contributes an additional0.00268555bpp per512crop and is not included here. The released gap mixes depth, training progress and provenance. Figure notes: Actual payload and the released-model gap Header excluded \u00b7 BD-rate uses each image\u2019s four-model common PSNR interval \u00b7 interim vs released comparison"
    }
  ],
